cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Cite this derivative software for the 200M-1B computational extension,
  and also cite Vranic's original software and lower-range data
  listed in references.
title: "Lerch primes: an audited computational extension from 200 million to one billion"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/nkKolja/lerch"
url: "https://github.com/nkKolja/lerch/releases/tag/results-1b-v1"
authors:
  - family-names: Kaluderovic
    given-names: Novak
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  An optimized ARM NEON and x86-64 AVX-512 implementation and reproducibility
  package for a completed search of all 39,768,597 primes above 200,000,000
  through 1,000,000,000, with no additional Lerch primes. Combined with the
  attributed upstream computation through 200,000,000, the known five Lerch
  primes exhaust the range through one billion. The evidence audit checks
  all saved archives, independently regenerated prime coverage and stored
  arithmetic identities, with additional arithmetic cross-checks at
  selected primes.
  The original MIT copyright and permission notice are preserved.
keywords:
  - Lerch primes
  - Fermat quotients
  - computational number theory
  - reproducibility
  - SIMD
